# UX Vocabulary

> **Do NOT invent — fill this by reading the real codebase and interviewing the team.**
> **Checklist before ANY visual work:**
> 1. Every action in the proposed UI appears in the Primary or Secondary actions table.
> 2. Every state the UI can be in appears in the States table.
> 3. Every surface the UI lives on appears in the Surfaces table.
> 4. All copy uses the voice defined in design-brief.md.
> If something is missing from this document, add it here FIRST, then design.

---

## Primary actions

> Actions the user takes that advance the core job-to-be-done.
> Fill by reading the main user flows in the codebase.

| Action | Where it appears | Input (what triggers it) | Outcome | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `<< action label >>` | `<< page / component >>` | `<< button click / form submit / … >>` | `<< what changes in the system >>` | `<< edge cases / constraints >>` |
| `<< action label >>` | `<< page / component >>` | `<< … >>` | `<< … >>` | `<< … >>` |

